  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'When blocks overflow, it does not immediately result in defense failure.

    Instead,
    75 CP is consumed to release the accumulated charge, dealing equivalent damage
    to the enemy and clearing all blocks

    (If the enemy is not defeated, existing
    enemy attacks will not be removed).


    Both row clears and Counter can accumulate
    charge.

    If CP is insufficient when overflow occurs, HP will be reduced to
    1, so the timing of overflow must be carefully considered from all angles.


    If
    the accumulated charge is sufficient to finish off the enemy,

    or if the
    board has become too unstable, deliberately allowing an overflow to wipe the
    field and deal massive damage can be a viable option.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c3202100722a9e245b5e57918ab2338e, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -598603385228235514, guid: c3202100722a9e245b5e57918ab2338e, type: 2}
